)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Commands -- Scrolling                    !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
{  UP, DOWN [amount]  }Scroll up or down (the Up and Down keys, PF7, PF8).
{  TOP, BOTTOM        }To the start or the end; BOT for short.
{  LEFT, RIGHT        }Sideways: the Left and Right keys, PF10 and PF11.
}                     Typed only on the log and output; lists: the keys.
}
}  The SCROLL field, right of the command line, holds the amount:
{  PAGE   }a screen          {  HALF   }half a screen
{  DATA   }a screen but one line, so one line stays in view
{  CSR    }the line of the cursor to the top
{  n      }n lines, up to 4 digits
}
}  The amount stays until you change it, also for the next session. A
}  word typed before a scroll key is the amount for that one scroll: M or
}  MAX to the end, P, H, D, C or a number. Typed UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT
}  take full words: DOWN MAX. Anything else: INVALID SCROLL AMOUNT.
}
}  The menu does not scroll.
}
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: commands   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFKPRT
  &ZUP = ISFKALL
)END
